Example of throw and throws across layers
class ExamService {
    void submit(String fileName, long sizeKb)
            throws ExamException {

        // Other exam and registration checks happen here.

        Storage storage = new Storage();
        storage.save(fileName, sizeKb);
    }
}

class ExamController {
    void submitAnswer(String fileName, long sizeKb) {
        ExamService service = new ExamService();

        try {
            service.submit(fileName, sizeKb);
            System.out.println("Submission completed.");
        }
        catch (ExamException e) {
            System.out.println("Submission rejected: "
                    + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}


Here, throw creates and sends an exception, while throws declares that a method may pass an exception to its caller.
